@title Frontend Framework Choice
@subtitle Rewriting the course-scheduling admin app
@author Internal Tools guild, Wrenfield University IT

The admin app has about 60 screens, mostly forms and tables, and 5 developers will build and maintain it. We compared React, Vue and Svelte.

## Criteria
- Team familiarity
- Form and table libraries
- Hiring pool
- Bundle size
- Long-term support

## Comparison
table = Framework,Team familiarity,Form/table ecosystem,Bundle size (KB),Hiring pool; React,4 of 5 developers,Excellent,142,Large; Vue,1 of 5 developers,Good,98,Medium; Svelte,0 of 5 developers,Fair,41,Small

## Pros and cons
### React
- Pro: 4 of 5 developers already know it
- Pro: excellent form and data-grid libraries
- Pro: largest hiring pool
- Con: largest bundle at 142 KB
### Vue
- Pro: smaller bundle at 98 KB
- Pro: good ecosystem
- Con: only 1 developer knows it
- Con: medium hiring pool
### Svelte
- Pro: smallest bundle at 41 KB
- Pro: favorite in the prototype spike
- Con: nobody on the team knows it
- Con: fair ecosystem and small hiring pool

## Recommendation
! **Choose React.** Four of the five developers already know it, and the data grid we need exists today.

> We are optimizing for the next five years of maintenance, not the first five weeks of building.
> — Hannah Osei, guild lead

Svelte was the favorite in the prototype spike, and we will revisit it for smaller tools.
